{"cut_proposal":{"candidate_errors":[],"prefix":"To solve the problem, we first need to determine the lengths of the diameters of the semi-circles and then calculate the areas of the shaded and unshaded regions in the semi-circle with diameter \\(AD\\).\n\nGiven the ratio \\(AB:BC:CD = 1:2:3\\), we can assign the lengths of the segments as follows:\n- Let \\(AB = x\\).\n- Then \\(BC = 2x\\).\n- And \\(CD = 3x\\).\n\nThe total length of \\(AD\\) is the sum of the lengths of \\(AB\\), \\(BC\\), and \\(CD\\):\n\\[\nAD = AB + BC + CD = x + 2x + 3x = 6x\n\\]\n\nThe diameter of the semi-circle with diameter \\(AD\\) is \\(6x\\), so its radius is:\n\\[\nr_{AD} = \\frac{6x}{2} = 3x\n\\]\n\nThe area of the semi-circle with diameter \\(AD\\) is:\n\\[\n\\text{Area of semi-circle with diameter } AD = \\frac{1}{2} \\pi (3x)^2 = \\frac{1}{2} \\pi (9x^2) = \\frac{9\\pi x^2}{2}\n\\]\n\nNext, we need to find the areas of the shaded and unshaded regions in this semi-circle. The shaded regions are the three semi-circles with diameters \\(AB\\), \\(BC\\), and \\(CD\\).\n\nThe radius of the semi-circle with diameter \\(AB\\) is:\n\\[\nr_{AB} = \\frac{x}{2} \\quad \\text{and its area is} \\quad \\frac{1}{2} \\pi \\left(\\frac{x}{2}\\right)^2 = \\frac{1}{2} \\pi \\left(\\frac{x^2}{4}\\right) = \\frac{\\pi x^2}{8}\n\\]\n\n","prefix_end":1178,"status":"review_required"},"eligible":true,"generation":{"generation":{"max_new_tokens":2048,"temperature":0.7,"top_k":0,"top_p":1.0},"ids":[1249,11625,279,3491,11,582,1156,1184,311,8253,279,28316,315,279,12757,2424,315,279,18267,1786,74263,323,1221,11047,279,5671,315,279,91766,323,650,927,14255,13604,304,279,18267,18664,448,23033,17767,1808,59,3593,22043,279,11341,17767,1867,25,4897,25,6484,284,220,16,25,17,25,18,59,701,582,646,9793,279,28316,315,279,20632,438,11017,510,12,6771,17767,1867,284,856,59,4292,12,5005,17767,4897,284,220,17,87,59,4292,12,1597,17767,6484,284,220,18,87,59,3593,785,2790,3084,315,17767,1808,57758,374,279,2629,315,279,28316,315,